{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/937903-cloud-infinite-2e-w-story-hook","id":937903,"title":"Cloud Infinite (2E) w/ story hook","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-26T20:30:59-07:00","id":937903,"title":"Cloud Infinite (2E) w/ story hook","content":"Hey all, first post here. Here's a Legacy import from 1E that I made in prep for my first ever Mage Chronicle. Unsure how it'll go in play, but I am rather proud of this one. I had to basically redesign the Legacy, formerly of Left Hand Path, for something more thematically and mechanically cohesive, because hey, Reapers should be using the Death Arcanum, and Mastigoi are the ones that exploit others because they're &quot;too weak&quot;. Idea was to make something of a technological vampire- one who just consumed Sleepers to fuel themselves because they were dealing with more important cognitive tasks. End result looks to be a <i>much </i>scarier Legacy and some potentially horrifying bad guys. Hope I kept within its spirit and within the rules- directly ported the oblations for one, and a lot of the general concept holds. Correct me if you feel I made a misstep.<br /> <br /> <b><i>The Cloud Infinite </i></b><br /> <br /> Nickname: Users<br /> Oblations: Solving mathetmatical problems in a group, collaborating on creative projects, building computer networks, making diagrams of social relationships<br /> Ruling Arcanum: Mind<br /> <br /> Yantras: Using a technological device in preparation for the spell (+1), reading a psychometric evaluation of a target before using a spell on them (+2), using stimulants to stay focused (+1, +2 w/ adverse Condition), mocking someone for intellectual inferiority (+1), successfully lying to someone (+2).<br /> <br /> <u><b>Origins</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Parentage</b>: Mastigos, Free Council or Seers of the Throne<br /> <br /> <b>Background</b>: Users are invariably gifted and privileged individuals who believe that their particularly strong intellect, especially affinity with technology, grants them license to command others. A classic example is that of the software mogul with a flashing, predatory smile, exhibiting some app they designed with a function of absolutely no significance to those outside of San Francisco Bay. They tend to espouse particularly odious social darwinian views, or are at least blankly ignorant about difficulties individuals may have had with systemic injustices.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance</b>: Users are sharply dressed, attractive, and successful. They exhibit the same joie de vivre and glib sense of humour as any other consummate sociopath. They have to, in order to get individuals around them to use their Attainments on. While a User could be a repugnant basement-dweller, they likely wouldn't be able to get enough people close enough to exploit them.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Doctrine</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Requirements</b>: Mind 2, Subterfuge or Occult 2, Computer or Empathy 2<br /> <br /> <b>Initiation</b>: There are generally two kinds of initiation among the Users. The first is that the student must display the kinds of ruthless calculation demanded by the Legacy's Attainments in a scenario designed by the mentor, for example, befriending and then undercutting a business competitor to gain an advantage on a negotiation, in which case the student is welcomed as a partner in crime. The second is that the mentor simply takes an impressionable Mage, explains their ferocious ability is a result of their highly exclusive Legacy, and lets them offer whatever material goods and services they can offer as a price, only informing them about its Left-Handed nature and sadistic Attainments once their Gnosis has been reshaped. The latter is more common than the former.<br /> <br /> <b>Organization: </b>It's perfectly conceivable that Users might work together on larger projects, and there would be many advantages to doing so, but there is only so long two sharks can stay in the same tank. Users are usurpers, and they know that about each other. Consequently they prefer to move apart and establish their own networks, once the student-mentor relationship is no longer of use.<br /> <br /> <b>Theory: </b>It is the right of the strong to use the weak. It is the weak's responsibility to become strong, and for the strong to become stronger. Only the truly brilliant can obtain success, as they are the only ones who deserve it.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Attainments</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>1st Attainment - Backup Diagnostics</b><br /> <i>Prerequisites: </i>Initiation<br /> A predator is useless without the ability to know their prey. The User can quickly size up an individual and how useful they might potentially become. With a touch, such as a long, firm handshake or playful pat on the back, they duplicate Know Nature, learning the target's Vice, Virtue and Mental and Social levels.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional - Death 1</b><br /> In addition to the cursory knowledge gleaned about the target's mentality, the User also learns about the state of their soul, per Soul Marks, such as if they've Awakened or are Possessed . However, the User must have more dots in Death than the target's Withstand rating, which uses Resolve, in order to obtain this information.<br /> <br /> <b>2nd Attainment - Exploit Spare Cycles</b><br /> <i>Prerequisites: </i>Mind 2, Subterfuge or Occult 3<br /> The User, having learnt just how much brainpower their companion is wasting, can use a variant of One Mind, Two Thoughts upon them with Advanced Duration. This can only be used on Sleepers or Sleepwalkers and must be initiated via touch, though the User can use the same physical contact of the first Attainment if they wish. During the course of this Attainment, the Sleeper does the User's thinking for them. They gain the <i>Overclocked </i>Condition.<br /> <br /> <i>Overclocked</i>: The character's spare mental capacity is being exploited by a User. During this time, they cannot use their own Willpower, though they may regain it as normal. Additionally, they suffer a -2 on any Mental or Social tasks not directly related to the User's goals. For example, noticing a truck running a red light will not be relevant to a User planning how to manipulate a government minister, though observing that same minister on television would be. The Sleeper often feels distracted or tired with this Condition, but there is no overt explanation for it.<br /> <br /> The User can spend the Willpower of the Overclocked individual on Mental and Social tasks, and can also multitask with a spell. There is a limitation however, in that the User can only use this Attainment up to as many individuals as they have Attainments overall. Thus a User who had the third Attainment could have this active on three different individuals.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional - Death 2 </b><br /> The User may spend a scene to create a Soul Jar out of a technological object with Advanced Duration.They may not bind souls to it without the Third Attainment, however. Additionally they can never spend Mana to make it Lasting. Hence the most common arrangement for active Users is a ring of disposable USB memory sticks.<br /> <br /> <b>3rd Attainment - Thought Administration </b><br /> <i>Prerequisites - </i>Mind 3, Computer or Empathy 3<br /> The User has learnt how to more effectively make use of Sleeper minds. Now, if the 2nd Attainment is active, they can use a variant of Psychic Domination to force the Overclocked Sleeper's mind to engage in a Teamwork roll on Mental or Social tasks, up to a number of tasks equal to the User's Mind dots. In the case of Extended Actions, each roll counts towards the limit. Once this is reached, the User must refresh it via touch. The User can force the Overclocked to use their Willpower for both their own rolls as well as the User's.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional - Death 3 </b><br /> Rather than using Psychic Domination on an Overclocked individual or refreshing its uses, the User can instead touch the Overclocked and tear out their soul, store it in one of their prepared Soul Jars, and use their Attainments on it as if it was the Sleeper themselves, provided they have Death dots greater than the Sleeper's Resolve. The subject of this Attainment is immediately afflicted with the Soulless Condition in addition to the Overclocked Condition, and begins the stages of Soul Loss. Should the User consume the Sleeper soul's Willpower through their 2nd Attainment the Sleeper suffers a Breaking Point at -3.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>4th Attainment - Soul Processing (1 Mana)</b><br /> <i>Prerequisites - </i>Mind 4, Subterfuge or Occult 4<br /> The User can drain the Mental or Social Attributes of a Sleeper or Sleeper souls via touch, in a variant of Augment Mind. They can take up to 4 dots from any Mental or Social category or combination of categories and add them to their own, up to their physical limits determined by Gnosis. This benefit lasts for 1 hour, after which time the gains fade, and the dots are, for the Sleeper, permanently and irrevocably lost. A Sleeper can be left with 0 dots in an attribute, usually leaving them catatonic or in a state of delirium, depending on the attribute.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional - Death 4 </b><br /> The User may shred one of their spare souls for extra Mana or Willpower, per Devouring the Slain, in conjunction with the above Mind effect. The damage inflicted appears on the original Sleeper as a withering effect, a physical torpor in addition to the malaise caused by the Soulless and Overclocked Conditions. This Attainment does count towards the number of times per day the Mage can gain Mana through scouring, however. Additionally it must overcome the Sleeper's Resolve, which Withstands it. However, most Users simply siphon the Resolve of the target beforehand.<br /> <br /> <b>5th Attainment - Into the Cloud</b><br /> <i>Prerequisites - </i>Mind 5, Computer or Empathy 4, all aforementioned skills at least 2.<br /> The User achieves a deeper enlightenment, and knows that there is no reason to limit their exploitation to the mind, when they have left a physical husk behind. The may use this Attainment to send their consciousness into a Sleeper who has been the subject of their 4th Attainment, per Possession. Possessing the soul of the target counts as Reach for the use of the Attainment within sensory range,but otherwise the User must touch the target. If the target is Enervated, they ignore the penalty for controlling the body of a living entity. If the target is a Thrall, they can choose to remain in that body indefinitely, potentially becoming a liche.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional - Death 5</b><br /> The User can use any of their Attainments on the Awakened.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hope that interests you. Spooks the heck out of me writing it up.<br /> <br /> Character hook (that I will be using in aforementioned Chronicle): A despicably cowardly Seer User of the Panopticon Ministry has been infected with the Nemesis Continuum (see Intruders). He has received Mystery Commands from the Exarchs instructing him that under no uncertain circumstances can he remove the Continuum via a simple mind wipe, instead he must find Abyssal relics and texts to find and conduct a rite that will extract the Continuum from him. He uses his Attainments on Sleepers and Sleepwalkers to boost his mental faculties so that he can complete his task and cope with the dual commands of the Exarchs and the Continuum, but fails to realise that his Legacy runs a high risk of spreading the Continuum to Sleepers and prompting sudden Abyssal manifestations throughout the Consilium.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12121-ainsoph","user":"AinSoph","date":". 07-27-2016, 08:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[